// Trust registry service (ADR-011). The service keeps one canonical trust
// entry per entity and publishes it through the etsi and dedi methods.
// The signed lists and the JWKS are standard HTTP GET endpoints, not RPCs
// (ADR-003 decision 7):
//   GET /trust/etsi/list.json serves the ETSI TS 119 602 JSON list as a JWS.
//   GET /.well-known/dedi.index.json serves the DeDi manifest.
//   GET /trust/dedi/<file> serves the DeDi directory files.
//   GET /.well-known/jwks.json serves the signing keys.

